{% doc %}
  blocks/_feature-card.liquid — private to `sections/feature-cards.liquid`.

  One feature: a title, a ringed icon and a line of text, with a picture that
  comes up under all three when a pointer is over the card.

  ## The card is a container, not a set of content settings

  It holds no words of its own. The title, the icon and the text are three
  nested blocks — `_feature-title`, `_feature-icon`, `_feature-text` — so the
  merchant decides the order, drops any one of them, or adds two lines of text
  under the icon, without this file knowing anything about it.

  That is the same split `blocks/_article-card.liquid` makes, for the same
  reason: a card whose parts are settings can only ever be the arrangement
  somebody chose while writing it.

  Unlike that one, this card is added by the merchant rather than rendered by
  the section, because a feature row's length is content — four things a store
  wants to say — not a count derived from a collection.

  ## The hover picture is decoration, and is marked as such

  It carries no alt text and sits in an `aria-hidden` layer. It is a mood behind
  words that are already on the page, and a screen reader announcing a filename
  in the middle of "Free delivery" is worse than silence. A merchant who has
  something to *say* with a picture wants an Image block, not this.

  There is always a layer: with no picture chosen it is Shopify's placeholder,
  through the same `snippets/image.liquid` call, so the hover works the moment
  the block is added and looks the way it will once a photograph replaces it.
  See the note by `has_placeholder`.

  It is also `pointer-events: none` in `base.css`, so the layer can never
  swallow a click meant for something inside the card.

  ## Why the hover colours live here and the icon's live in the icon

  The card owns what the card paints — its picture, its overlay, the colour the
  words turn when the picture is behind them. The disc, the ring and the glyph
  are the icon block's box, so their hover colours are its settings.

  The line that reads across — `.feature-card:hover .feature-icon-block__disc`
  — is in the icon's own part of the stylesheet, not the card's. A block still
  styles only its own box; it is allowed to know which state the card is in.

  ## Touch has no hover, so the hover state is simply on

  Every hover rule sits inside `@media (hover: hover)`, and `base.css` carries
  the exact inverse — an `@media (hover: none)` block that makes the same state
  the resting one. On a phone the picture is up, the tint is on and the words
  are already in their second colour.

  That is the opposite of the usual advice, and it is the right answer here
  because of what is behind the hover. This is not a control that reveals an
  action; it is a photograph, a tint and a colour — content. Content a phone can
  never reach is content that does not exist on a phone, and half the card would
  simply be missing there. The alternative is worse than the sticky `:hover` it
  avoids: an unguarded rule latches after a tap and stays until the customer
  taps elsewhere, which reads as a bug, while a permanent state reads as design.

  The one exception is the icon's rotation, which stays keyed to a tap. See the
  note in `blocks/_feature-icon.liquid`.

  The condition is `max-width: 749px` **or** `(hover: none)`, not either alone.
  `(hover: none)` is the honest test for a phone, but the theme editor's mobile
  preview is a narrow viewport in a desktop browser with a mouse attached — it
  reports `hover: hover`, and on that test alone a merchant laying out the
  mobile view was shown a card no phone would render.

  `:focus-within` is paired with `:hover` throughout, so a keyboard reaching a
  link inside the card gets the same state a pointer does.

  ## Every default is written twice, and both are load-bearing

  The schema default, and the Liquid fallback beside the setting that reads it:

      "id": "min_height", "default": 400
      assign min_height = s.min_height | default: 400 | plus: 0

  They have to agree. Where they disagreed, the Liquid one won for any card
  whose settings had not been stored — a card with no `min_height` in its JSON
  read the `| default: 0` here, not the 400 in the schema, and sized itself to
  its content while the panel showed 400 in the editor.

  The section preset is the third copy and the one that made this visible. A
  preset block with no `settings` object at all — the only such block in this
  file's preset, and the only one whose settings did not apply — is created with
  nothing stored, so every card fell through to the Liquid fallbacks at once:
  no padding, square corners, no overlay, no minimum height.

  `sections/featured-blog.liquid` writes the settings on every block in its
  preset for this reason. So does this one now. **Adding a setting here means
  adding it in three places**, and the audit that catches a miss is comparing
  the schema defaults against the `| default:` filters in this file.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign align = s.alignment | default: 'center'
  assign gap = s.gap | default: 16 | plus: 0
  assign min_height = s.min_height | default: 400 | plus: 0

  comment
    Same border resolution the section frame uses, down to the four widths.

    One width per side rather than one for the box: the frame a merchant wants
    on a card is often a single rule — a rail down the left of each feature, or
    a line between the row and what follows it — and a single slider could only
    ever draw all four or none. They are summed into `border_any` so the three
    properties are emitted only when at least one side is actually drawn; a
    zero-width border with a colour on it is three declarations that paint
    nothing and one that overrides the component's own CSS.

    A blank colour resolves to `currentColor` faded with `color-mix` rather than
    through `color_modify`: the colour filters need a value to read an alpha
    channel off, and there is nothing to read until the scheme resolves in the
    browser.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'
  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0
  assign border_paint = ''

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    A phone gets its own corner because the same number does not read the same
    at both widths — 24px is a soft round on a 312px card and a heavy scoop out
    of one that is nearly the full width of a 390px screen. `| default: radius`
    rather than a constant, so a card saved before the mobile slider existed
    keeps one shape at every width. Same pair, same reasoning, as the section's.
  endcomment
  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign radius_mobile = s.border_radius_mobile | default: radius | plus: 0

  assign background_paint = ''
  if s.background_color != blank
    assign background_alpha = s.background_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    assign background_alpha = background_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | color_modify: 'alpha', background_alpha
  endif

  comment
    ---- the hover layer ----

    The overlay is a colour with the slider folded into its alpha rather than an
    element at `opacity`, because an element's opacity would fade the picture
    *and* anything a merchant later puts in the same layer. One `background`
    with an alpha channel fades exactly the tint.
  endcomment
  comment
    There is always a hover layer. With no picture uploaded it is Shopify's
    placeholder, rendered through `snippets/image.liquid` like any other
    image — same `<responsive-image>` wrapper, same fade-in, same load
    behaviour — so the hover works out of the box and the merchant can see what
    they are configuring before they have chosen a photograph.

    That matters most in the theme editor, which is where this section is
    judged: a card whose hover does nothing until a picture is uploaded reads as
    a broken setting rather than as an empty one. It is the same call
    `sections/featured-blog.liquid` makes when it draws placeholder cards for a
    blog with no posts.

    `has_placeholder` is kept separate from `has_media` because the two answer
    different questions — one decides what to render, the other whether the card
    is showing the merchant's own content. `base.css` gives the placeholder a
    ground of its own so the overlay has something to tint; it does not lighten
    the overlay, because the question the merchant is asking of the preview is
    whether white words will sit on a dark picture.
  endcomment
  assign has_media = true
  assign has_placeholder = false
  if s.hover_image == blank
    assign has_placeholder = true
  endif

  comment
    ---- what the picture does while it is up ----

    Zoom is a hover effect and Drift is a scroll effect, which is why they are
    one select rather than a pair of toggles: they animate the same `transform`
    on the same layer, and two controls able to ask for both would resolve to
    whichever declaration came last in the stylesheet.

    Drift is `<parallax-media>`, the element the hero already uses, rather than
    `motion-effect data-effect="parallax"`, which `snippets/background-image.liquid`
    uses. The two are different mechanisms: motion-effect translates the element
    itself and needs 120px of overscan around it — a number coupled by hand to a
    clamp in `assets/motion-engine.js` — while `<parallax-media>` writes
    `--parallax-offset` and lets CSS combine it with a `scale()`, which covers
    the travel with no second number to keep in step. A layer that already fills
    its box wants the second one.

    The speed is converted here, not passed through. The engine wants a
    multiplier and the schema stores a percentage a merchant can reason about;
    handing 30 to a function that clamps at 0.5 pins every card to maximum
    strength and the effect stops responding to the slider.
    `snippets/background-image.liquid` documents this as the bug it had.

    (`sections/hero-banner.liquid` still passes its percentage straight through
    and is pinned at the clamp. Not touched from here — it is its own file and
    its own fix.)
  endcomment
  assign image_effect = s.hover_image_effect | default: 'zoom_in'

  assign image_scale = s.hover_image_scale | default: 110 | plus: 0
  assign image_scale = image_scale | divided_by: 100.0

  assign drift_speed = s.hover_image_parallax_speed | default: 30 | plus: 0
  if drift_speed < 10
    assign drift_speed = 10
  endif
  if drift_speed > 50
    assign drift_speed = 50
  endif
  assign drift_speed = drift_speed | divided_by: 100.0

  assign layer_tag = 'div'
  if image_effect == 'drift'
    assign layer_tag = 'parallax-media'
  endif

  assign overlay_paint = ''
  assign overlay_tint = s.overlay_color | default: '#000000'
  if overlay_tint != blank
    assign overlay_alpha = s.overlay_opacity | default: 60 | plus: 0
    assign overlay_alpha = overlay_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign overlay_paint = overlay_tint | color_modify: 'alpha', overlay_alpha
  endif

  comment
    The hover text colour is a class as well as a property. Emitting the
    property alone and writing `color: var(--feature-card-hover-text, inherit)`
    would mean an unset colour resolving to `inherit` on hover — which is not
    "leave it alone", it is "override whatever the title block set on itself".
    So the rule only exists when the merchant has asked for it.
  endcomment
  assign hover_text = s.hover_text_color | default: '#FFFFFF'

  assign card_classes = 'feature-card feature-card--align-' | append: align
  if has_media
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' feature-card--has-media'
  endif
  if has_placeholder
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' feature-card--placeholder-media'
  endif
  if hover_text != ''
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' feature-card--hover-text'
  endif

  comment
    `sizes` describes the widest this picture is ever painted. A feature card is
    a quarter of the row on a desktop and close to the full width of a phone, so
    a wrong hint here is the usual cause of a hover picture arriving three sizes
    too large for the box it fills.
  endcomment
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 990px) 25vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 90vw'
-%}

{%- capture card_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --feature-card-gap: {{ gap }}px;
  --feature-card-align: {{ align }};
  --feature-card-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --feature-card-radius-mobile: {{ radius_mobile }}px;
  --feature-card-transition: {{ s.hover_duration | default: 500 | plus: 0 }}ms;
  --feature-card-lift: {{ s.hover_lift | default: 0 | plus: 0 }}px;
  {%- if min_height > 0 -%}
    --feature-card-min-height: {{ min_height }}px;
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --feature-card-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --feature-card-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --feature-card-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    --feature-card-background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if overlay_paint != '' -%}
    --feature-card-overlay: {{ overlay_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if hover_text != '' -%}
    --feature-card-hover-text: {{ hover_text }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if image_effect == 'zoom_in' or image_effect == 'zoom_out' -%}
    --feature-card-image-scale: {{ image_scale }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="{{ card_classes }}"
  data-block-spacing
  style="{{ card_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Decoration, and marked as such — see the note above. `alt: ''` as well as
    `aria-hidden` on the layer, because the two are read by different things and
    a filename announced mid-sentence is worse than nothing.

    One render call for both states. `snippets/image.liquid` draws the
    placeholder itself when `image` is blank, so there is no second branch here
    that could hold a different wrapper, a different `sizes` hint or a different
    fade — which is how a placeholder ends up animating unlike the picture that
    replaces it.

    `hero-apparel-1` rather than the flat grey mark: the apparel family is the
    set this theme uses everywhere an empty slot appears, so a section being
    configured looks like the same store as the one next to it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="feature-card__media" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- comment -%}
      One inner layer, whichever effect is on it — a `<div>` for none and the
      two zooms, `<parallax-media>` for Drift. The class is the same either way,
      so the sizing rules in `base.css` do not have to know which element they
      got, and the modifier is the only thing that varies.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <{{ layer_tag }}
      class="feature-card__layer feature-card__layer--{{ image_effect | replace: '_', '-' }}"
      {% if image_effect == 'drift' %}data-speed="{{ drift_speed }}"{% endif %}
    >
      {% render 'image',
         image: s.hover_image,
         mobile_image: s.hover_image_mobile,
         alt: '',
         class: 'feature-card__image',
         placeholder: 'hero-apparel-1',
         sizes: card_sizes %}
    </{{ layer_tag }}>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-card__inner">
    {% content_for 'blocks' %}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.feature_card.name",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "_feature-title" },
    { "type": "_feature-icon" },
    { "type": "_feature-text" },
    { "type": "@app" }
  ],
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:blocks.feature_card.paragraph" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.article_card.settings.gap.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.gap.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.min_height.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.min_height.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 640,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 400
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.feature_card.headers.hover" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:blocks.feature_card.paragraphs.hover" },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "hover_image",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "hover_image_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.hover_image != blank }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "overlay_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_color.label",
      "default": "#000000"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "overlay_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 60
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "hover_image_effect",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_effect.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_effect.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "zoom_in", "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_effect.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "zoom_out", "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_effect.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "drift", "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_effect.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "zoom_in"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hover_image_scale",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_scale.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_scale.info",
      "min": 100,
      "max": 140,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 110,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.hover_image_effect == 'zoom_in' or block.settings.hover_image_effect == 'zoom_out' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hover_image_parallax_speed",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_parallax_speed.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_image_parallax_speed.info",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 30,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.hover_image_effect == 'drift' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "hover_text_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_text_color.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_text_color.info",
      "default": "#FFFFFF"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hover_duration",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_duration.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_duration.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1200,
      "step": 50,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 500
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hover_lift",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_lift.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.hover_lift.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.appearance.header" },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.appearance.background_color.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.background_color.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "background_opacity",
      "label": "t:sections.feature_cards.settings.panel_background_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.background_color != blank }}"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.borders" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:blocks.feature_card.paragraphs.borders" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:shared.border.style.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:shared.options.solid" },
        { "value": "dashed", "label": "t:shared.options.dashed" }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width_top",
      "label": "t:shared.border.sides.top.label",
      "info": "t:shared.border.sides.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width_right",
      "label": "t:shared.border.sides.right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.border.sides.bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width_left",
      "label": "t:shared.border.sides.left.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.border.opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "t:shared.border.color.label",
      "info": "t:shared.border.color.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "label": "t:shared.corners.radius.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.border_radius.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.corners.radius_mobile.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.spacing.block_header" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:shared.spacing.block_paragraph" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 40,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
